  {
    "file": "learner/briefs/philosophy.pavement-saves-nature.md.min",
    "lines": [
      "# philosophy: pavement saves nature 🦉🗿🌱",
      "",
      "> **pavement saves nature.**",
      "",
      "one claim, true at two scales: the **why** under every externalization rule the learner carries, and under the rule to *read* what is already there.",
      "",
      "## the bridge — where the metaphor turns literal",
      "",
      "**pavement is reusable prethought** — a brief, a howto, a term cluster, a resolved dispute, a paved route. somebody already spent the energy, and wrote the result where the next traveler picks it up for the cost of a read.",
      "",
      "\`\`\`",
      "reuse the pavement → do not re-derive → do not re-spend the energy → save nature",
      "\`\`\`",
      "",
      "## the asymmetry — this is what makes it compound",
      "",
      "| | cost | paid by |",
      "|---|---|---|",
      "| **pave it** | once | the first traveler |",
      "| **improvise it** | every time | every traveler, forever |",
      "",
      "⇒ so *"write more briefs"* is **not** the lesson. it is *"write the ones that will be walked, and then walk them."*",
      "",
      "## 🟡 the two failures",
      "",
      "| failure | shape | correction |",
      "|---|---|---|",
      "| **the braided trail** | a second path laid beside a serviceable one, because the author did not look | check the pavement before you lay more |",
      "| **the rut** | conformity to a found path, with no test of whether it leads anywhere | check that the pavement is not a rut |",
      "",
      "⇒ **precedent is a reason to look, never a reason to conform.**",
      "",
      "⇒ the repair for both: **do not widen the braid — mend the tread.** if a paved path is genuinely bad, **fix the pavement**; do not walk beside it.",
      "",
      "a traveler who must think **should think**; offroad exploration is honest work. the philosophy asks one move first: **check for a path** — and when none exists, walk it and **leave a route behind**.",
      "",
      "> pave it once, so it is never paid for twice.",
      "> then **walk it** — an unwalked path is the only wasted one. 🦉🗿🌱",
    ],
  },
  {
    "file": "learner/briefs/rule.always.archive-the-wishers-words-verbatim.md.min",
    "lines": [
      "# rule.always.archive-the-wishers-words-verbatim",
      "",
      "when the wisher says a word that **changes the work**, catch it verbatim before you distill it.",
      "",
      "\`\`\`",
      "$route/.seeds/inventory.of=seeds._.md                # the SUMMARY — the axis, the counts, the gaps",
      "$route/.seeds/inventory.of=seeds.case=S$n-$slug.md   # one ENTRY per utterance",
      "\`\`\`",
      "",
      "both are owed, every time.",
      "",
      "| when the wisher… | then |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| settles a question | archive it — future rounds inherit the settlement |",
      "| 🔴 **corrects you** | the highest-value quote there is: it records the wrong path AND the right one |",
      "| coins a word or a convention | the coinage's source is its etymology |",
      "| specifies a contract verbatim — a path, a flag, a format | a specification paraphrased is a specification changed |",
      "| 🔴 **asks a question** whose answer changes the work | the cheapest kind to lose — in hindsight it reads as though YOU found the gap |",
      "| — or you are about to write *"the wisher asked for…"* | that citation needs a source. archive first |",
      "",
      "a seed holds \`.said\` · \`.settled\` · \`.landed\`.",
      "",
      "| repair it | never touch it |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| a **typo** — a transposed letter, a dropped one, a doubled word | a word choice, however informal |",
      "| **profanity** — cut it, or swap in a neutral \`[placeholder]\`. never a softened or masked form of the word | the order the points arrive in |",
      "| a mangled path, flag, or identifier, where the intent is plain | a mid-thought correction — that IS the record |",
      "",
      "🟡 **\`.said\` is verbatim in SUBSTANCE — repair the surface.** the words, their order, their emphasis, and their mid-thought corrections stay unedited; **typos and profanity are repaired.**",
      "",
      "🔴 the test: would the speaker, shown both, say *"that is what I typed, spelled right"*? yes → a repair. a change past that is a rewrite, and a rewrite belongs in \`.settled\`.",
      "",
      "## 🔴 a seed is the seed of a CONCEPT, never a chronicle of the round",
      "",
      "\`.settled\` states what now HOLDS. strip every reference to this route, its tools, its fulcrums, and its errors — **does the concept still stand?** what survives is the seed; the rest is archaeology, and git already holds it.",
      "",
      "🟡 the tell: a \`.landed\` list longer than the concept, whose rows carry a REASON rather than a path.",
      "",
      "## 🔴 the ENVIRONMENT is not a seed",
      "",
      "a channel's switch state, a credential's health, a tool broken that day — real, and a directive for the session, never a concept a future traveler inherits. **strip the machinery; if naught is left, drop it.**",
      "",
      "blocker: an utterance that changed the work with no seed · a \`"the wisher asked for X"\` with no source · a \`.said\` whose SENSE was edited · a \`.said\` that ships a typo or profanity · profanity persisted whole or as a masked or softened form (a neutral \`[placeholder]\` is fine) · entries with no summary · a bare-ordinal \`case=\` · a body that narrates the round · a \`.landed\` row that carries a reason · a durable concept with no brief behind it.",
    ],
  },
  {
    "file": "learner/briefs/rule.always.catch-dreams-for-followups.md.min",
    "lines": [
      "# rule.always.catch-dreams-for-followups",
      "",
      "> **every followup you do not do becomes a caught dream — and the route that found it keeps a symlink to it.**",
      "",
      "🟡 first run the SAFE/CLEAN test (\`rule.always.fix-forward-under-scouts-honor\`) — its PAIR, booted beside it here.",
      "",
      "- a dream is the second-best outcome: safe and clean means fix it now, and no dream is owed",
      "- ⇒ this rule governs what the large half owes",
      "- ⇒ a role that holds this half alone inverts the default and reads the dream as the primary move",
      "  - so the pair boots together, always: a role that carries one carries both",
      "",
      "the shape and the four kinds are the \`dream\` contract — \`term=artifact.dream._.choice._.md\`.",
      "",
      "## .why — a spoken followup is a deletion in a polite coat",
      "",
      "| kept by a dream | why it matters |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| the cue that fired | *what made you notice* is what a later reader cannot reconstruct |",
      "| the reason it was deferred | so the next traveler does not re-derive the judgment and defer again |",
      "| the shape of the fix | you held the context. that comprehension is the expensive half |",
      "",
      "## 🔴 .why the symlink",
      "",
      "\`\`\`sh",
      "rhx symlink --at "$route/dreams/v$date.$kind.$slug.md" \\",
      "            --to ".dream/v$date.$kind.$slug.md" \\",
      "            --mode relative --idem findsert",
      "\`\`\`",
      "",
      "🟡 a deferral for DIRT owes a FULCRUM too.",
      "",
      "- the dream records the work; the fulcrum records the decision to defer it",
      "- a dream alone reports the work and hides the call",
      "- ⇒ and the ripple estimate that made it dirty is a best guess, which is what a fulcrum list exists to surface",
      "",
      "| when… | then… |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| you would say *"i'll flag that for later"* | 🔴 that phrase IS the cue. run the two questions, then fix it or catch it |",
      "| a rule you just wrote fires on your very next action and you route around it | 🔴 the sharpest cue. the rule found a real gap and you skipped it |",
      "| you hit a broken paved path — a documented command that fails, a stale readme | catch it. a documented defect is worse than an absent doc |",
      "| a fix belongs to another repo | catch it as a \`reseed\` dream. a tree adopts only what is scoped to itself |",
      "| you cannot push a seed | 🔴 \`.dream/\` is the local queue. caught is not dispatched |",
      "| a fix is large — a rename across files, a contract change, a migration | catch it, with the shape of the fix |",
      "| you finish a route with an empty \`$route/dreams/\` | 🔴 suspicious. a real round finds at least one item it could not clean |",
      "",
      "## .the shape",
      "",
      "\`# 🌙 dream: $what-is-owed\` · kind · owner · caught $date, then: \`.the cue that fired\` · \`.the gap, precisely\` (with checkable evidence) · \`.the shape of the fix\` · \`.why it is not done in this round\` (the SAFE/CLEAN answer).",
      "",
      "blocker: a followup mentioned and never caught · a dream caught for a fix that was safe and clean (that was a fix) · a dream with no symlink at the route that found it · a dream that lives inside a route rather than \`.dream/\` · a dirt deferral with no fulcrum. nitpick: no \`.the shape of the fix\`.",
    ],
  },
  {
    "file": "learner/briefs/rule.always.enskill-the-tactics-you-discover.md.min",
    "lines": [
      "# rule.always.enskill-the-tactics-you-discover",
      "",
      "**when you repeat a sequence of operations, that sequence is a tactic, and it is owed a skill.**",
      "",
      "this is the DISCOVER half. \`rule.always.entool-the-skills-you-touch\` is the UPGRADE half. one loop:",
      "",
      "\`\`\`",
      "discover a repeated sequence → ENSKILL it → notice the leftover brain work → ENTOOL it",
      "\`\`\`",
      "",
      "| when… | then… |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| you ran the **same sequence a second time** | 🔴 the strongest cue. enskill it now — the repeat already proved it |",
      "| you **scroll back to copy a command** you ran earlier | your scrollback does a skill's job |",
      "| you chain 3+ commands where each feeds the next | the chain is one tactic, not three steps |",
      "| you **explain a procedure** to someone (or a future self) | you just spoke the skill aloud — write it |",
      "| you think *"the trick is to run X before Y"* | that order constraint is exactly the knowledge worth capture |",
      "| you keep a **private note** of steps | a private note is an unshared skill |",
      "| a sequence is **easy to run and hard to recall** | the highest-value case |",
      "| the steps need **judgment at several points**, in an order that matters | 🗿 **pave a route**, not a linear skill |",
      "| you went **offroad** and reached the end | the path you found IS the artifact. leave a route behind |",
      "",
      "## .the test",
      "",
      "> **"could the next traveler run this without me in the room?"**",
      "",
      "- yes, from what is written → enskilled",
      "- yes, **but they would ask me one question** → **that question is the whole point.** it marks the undiscoverable step",
      "- no, judgment at **one** point → leave it with the brain, and say so",
      "- no, judgment at **several** points, in an order that matters → 🗿 **a route**",
      "",
      "then: **"how much could run with no brain at all?"** — write it at that rung today, not the fluid version out of haste.",
      "",
      "## 🗿 .when brains are required along the way — pave a route",
      "",
      "⇒ **a skill paves a sequence of commands. a route paves a sequence of judgments.**",
      "",
      "and **do not route what could be entooled** — a route around deterministic work charges imagine cost at every stone.",
      "",
      "**offroad is legitimate — and it owes a route.** the exploration happened anyway; to end it with pavement turns a one-time cost into a permanent asset.",
      "",
      "## .what a skill owes",
      "",
      "idempotent · named for the **motive**, not the mechanism · fails loud and names the fix · discoverable via \`--help\` · **owned by the right tree** — a tactic whose home is another repo is re-seeded there.",
      "",
      "## .anti-patterns",
      "",
      "the third repeat by hand · the scrollback tactic · the private note · **the premature skill** (run once, enskilled from a guess — wait for the second run) · **the offroad trip with no pavement left behind**.",
      "",
      "blocker: a procedure explained with no durable artifact · an offroad exploration that reached its end and left no route. nitpick: written at 💧 where 🔩 was in reach · a route laid over deterministic work.",
    ],
  },
  {
    "file": "learner/briefs/rule.always.entool-the-skills-you-touch.md.min",
    "lines": [
      "# rule.always.entool-the-skills-you-touch",
      "",
      "**when you use a skill and a brain still has to do part of the job, that leftover brain work is a defect in the TOOL, not a duty of the caller.** name it, and upsert the skill one rung closer to a single deterministic call.",
      "",
      "this is the WATCH half. \`rule.always.externalize.tactics.into_skills\` says *write the skill*; this says *the written skill is 💧 fluid — rung 2 of 4*, and it is the learner's permanent job to notice which rung each skill it touches actually sits on.",
      "",
      "| when… | then… |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| you call a skill, **then** run a command to finish what it started | the follow-up belongs **inside** the skill |",
      "| you call a skill and **read its output to decide** the next call | that decision is a candidate branch inside the tool |",
      "| you call the same two skills in the same order, twice | the pair wants **one** call |",
      "| you must **read a skill's instructions** to know what to run | it is rung 2. ask what 🔩 rigid looks like |",
      "| its output must be **reshaped** before the next step | fix the seam, not the caller |",
      "| you write a **new** skill | write it at the highest rung you can defend today |",
      "| a skill **fails** and you work around it by hand | 🔴 the strongest signal there is — never leave it unnamed |",
      "",
      "## .the test — answer BOTH",
      "",
      "> **1. "what did I still have to figure out myself, after that one call?"**",
      "",
      "naught → rung 4 🪨, leave it. one or more steps → each is an unclimbed rung.",
      "",
      "🟡 **name the WORK, not a count of turns.** two turns can differ by orders of magnitude in time, tokens, and risk.",
      "",
      "> **2. "is that leftover step a JUDGMENT, or a STEP?"**",
      "",
      "- a **judgment** — weighs an ambiguous case, reads intent, decides a tradeoff → **leave it with the brain.** never fake determinism over judgment",
      "- a **step** — the same every time, and you could write down exactly what you did → **it is owed a tool**",
      "",
      "## .what to do with what you found",
      "",
      "small and entoolable now → **do it now** · real work → write it where the next traveler finds it (a seed, or a catch in \`.dream/\`) · a judgment → say so explicitly; a documented *"this stays with the brain, because X"* is a real artifact that stops a fake-tool attempt.",
      "",
      "**a skill owned by another repo is re-seeded, never entooled here.**",
      "",
      "## .anti-patterns",
      "",
      "**the silent glue** — you do the leftover step by hand every time and never name it; invisible precisely because you are good at the close · **the fake tool** — determinism asserted over a fluid process; worse than the brain it replaced, because a brain hesitates and a bad tool does not · **💧 fluid forever** · **the workaround that outlives its defect**.",
      "",
      "blocker: a manual workaround for a broken skill, unrecorded · a tool that asserts determinism over a genuine judgment. ⇒ \`philosophy.entoolment-is-the-pinnacle\` is the why.",
      "",
      "> if you finished the job by hand, the tool is not finished. 🦉🔧",
    ],
  },
