    "file": "learner/briefs/rule.forbid.domain-term-inconsistency.md.min",
    "lines": [
      "# rule.forbid.domain-term-inconsistency",
      "",
      "no single concept may be named with more than one word across the codebase. where two or more words name the **same** concept and **no canonical term has yet been declared**, the vocabulary is inconsistent — and the inconsistency is forbidden.",
      "",
      "⇒ this is the **pre-canon twin** of \`rule.forbid.domain-term-synonyms\`. that rule forbids a drift away from a term already declared canonical; this one forbids the codebase from a disagreement with **itself**, before any canon exists.",
      "",
      "test: **"is this concept named the same way everywhere it appears?"** one word → consistent · two or more → coin the canonical term, conform the rest.",
      "",
      "## .how",
      "",
      "1. **confirm they are truly one concept** — not a real distinction concealed under a shared shape",
      "2. choose the canonical word (\`howto.domain-term-disputes\` when it is arguable)",
      "3. itemize it (\`rule.require.domain-term-itemization\`); conform the other uses, or **leave them until disturbed** — no forced mass-rewrite",
      "",
      "> one concept, one word — even before the glossary names it 📜",
      "",
      "blocker: a single concept named with two or more words across contracts, with no canonical term declared.",
    ],
  },
