    "file": "learner/briefs/rule.forbid.domain-term-synonyms.md.min",
    "lines": [
      "# rule.forbid.domain-term-synonyms",
      "",
      "no **contract** may use a synonym of a term declared in \`domain.terms/\`. use the canonical term, or open a dispute.",
      "",
      "a **contract** = a dobj/dop name, an internal contract (input/output shapes, signatures), and **above all the external interfaces we publish** (api, sdk, cli). a synonym there is the violation.",
      "",
      "a **comment** may use a synonym to describe the concept from an alternate perspective — that is allowed. the term's \`choice._.md\` records the forbidden synonyms, so the canonical map stays clear.",
      "",
      "## .how — adhere, or dispute",
      "",
      "1. **adhere** — rename the contract to the canonical term, or",
      "2. **dispute** — if you believe the synonym is right (or names a genuinely distinct concept), open a dated entry in the term's \`choice.reason.md\` (\`howto.domain-term-disputes\`)",
      "",
      "touch a contract that already carries a forbidden synonym → clean it up. but it may be **left in place until disturbed** — no forced mass-rewrite.",
      "",
      "test: **"is this synonym in a CONTRACT, or in a COMMENT?"** contract → adhere or dispute · comment → allowed.",
      "",
      "> one concept, one word — everywhere a contract can be read 📜",
      "",
      "blocker: a synonym of a declared term used in a dobj/dop name, an internal contract, or a published external interface.",
    ],
  },
