    "file": "learner/briefs/rule.require.enumerate-before-you-name.md.min",
    "lines": [
      "# rule.require.enumerate-before-you-name",
      "",
      "> **list every instance the word must cover. THEN pick the word.**",
      "",
      "## .the two failure modes — one instance hides both",
      "",
      "| failure | what it looks like | why one instance cannot catch it |",
      "|---|---|---|",
      "| **too narrow** | fits the case you looked at, breaks on a case you never listed | you never listed it |",
      "| **too wide** | fits every case — so it discriminates none of them | with one case, *"it fits"* reads as success |",
      "",
      "## .the test — forced articulation, before the word",
      "",
      "> **1. "what are ALL the instances this word must cover?"**",
      "> **2. "does the candidate cover every one — and does it EXCLUDE its neighbours?"**",
      "",
      "- a row it does not cover → **too narrow.** widen, or split into two words",
      "- covers every row **and** every adjacent concept → **too wide.** it is the genus; you need the differentia",
      "- covers every row and excludes the neighbours → the word holds",
      "",
      "## .the worked case — \`degenerate\` vs \`specialized\`",
      "",
      "| the rung-3 shape | \`degenerate\`? | a \`specialization\`? |",
      "|---|---|---|",
      "| a skill that computes its setup, then hands one probabilistic step to a brain | ✅ a route reduced to **one stone** | ✅ |",
      "| a wrapper that batches the deterministic half | 🔴 **no** — an all-deterministic route is complete, not reduced | ✅ |",
      "",
      "## .the peer cases — the same test, the opposite failure",
      "",
      "| the word | the list showed |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| \`knowledge\`, to contrast a **brief** | covers **both** — a skill carries knowledge too. it is the genus; \`concepts\` / \`capacity\` are the differentia |",
      "| \`tool\`, to contrast a **brief** | covers **all four** rungs, so it cannot also name a proper subset. \`skill\` is the contrast word |",
      "| \`rung\`, unqualified | **one word, two senses** — a review gate and a determinism position. the flat namespace has one slot; the list needs two |",
      "",
      "| when… | then… |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| you name a **relation** between two concepts | 🔴 list every pair the word must hold over, first |",
      "| a word fits the example you have in view | that is a sample of one. what is the second? |",
      "| you reach for a **term of art** because it is precise | precision is what makes it narrow. check the rows it excludes |",
      "| a candidate covers **every** instance you listed | 🔴 check the **adjacent concepts** too — a word that covers them all is the genus |",
      "| you cannot list a second instance | the concept may not be general enough to earn a word yet |",
      "",
      "⇒ this **precedes** the glossary rules: \`rule.forbid.domain-term-synonyms\` asks *"one concept or two?"*, which is this enumeration applied to senses; \`rule.require.boundary-qualified-terms\` catches the \`rung\` case **after** two senses exist. this is where both are cheapest — at authorship, with a table, before a citation exists.",
      "",
      "blocker: a term proposed with **one** instance cited · an enumeration that shows an uncovered row · a term that covers every row **and** its neighbours. false positive: a concept that genuinely has one instance — say so, and why a second is unavailable.",
    ],
  },
  {
    "file": "learner/briefs/rule.require.specialize-a-rule-its-readers-look-past._.md.min",
    "lines": [
      "# rule.require.specialize-a-rule-its-readers-look-past",
      "",
      "> **a rule whose every example draws from one domain will be read as a rule ABOUT that domain.**",
      "",
      "when a reader violates a general rule in a **second** domain, the repair is **not** a louder \`.what\`. it is a **named specialization** — a peer rule, in the domain the reader occupied, that states the same claim in that domain's own words and cites the general rule as its parent.",
      "",
      "## 🟡 .the honest bound",
      "",
      "⇒ a split is the **first** move, never the last. a rule looked past **after** it was specialized has earned a mechanism, and the specialization is what tells you which situation the mechanism must fire in.",
      "",
      "| when… | then… |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| you write a general rule and **every example is from one domain** | 🔴 the split is owed **at authorship**, not after the first violation |",
      "| a reader violates it **in a domain it does not illustrate** | specialize into **their** domain; do not bold the parent |",
      "| you would **bold, widen, or warn** after a miss | ask first whether the reader ever recognized the rule applied |",
      "| a rule reaches a second domain and you add a **second example** | cheaper and weaker. weigh a named peer instead |",
      "| you name a specialization | name it in the **reader's** vocabulary, never the parent's |",
      "",
      "test: **"in what situation would a reader who AGREES with this rule fail to notice it applies?"** — you can name one → that situation is the specialization, and it is owed.",
      "",
      "## .what a specialization owes",
      "",
      "the **specialization**: the claim in the reader's own domain vocabulary, its own concrete examples, and a \`.see also\` pointer **up**. the **parent**: a pointer **down**, plus one line on **why** the split happened — the dated miss.",
      "",
      "## 🟡 .NOT a license to fork a rule per domain",
      "",
      "| the situation | the move |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| a reader **looked past** it in a second domain — evidenced | **specialize** |",
      "| a reader **read** it and disagreed | argue the rule; a peer changes no mind |",
      "| you **anticipate** a second domain, no reader, no miss | add an example. wait for the evidence |",
      "",
      "⇒ **the trigger is a real reader who looked past it.**",
      "",
      "blocker: a general rule single-domain-illustrated, after a reader violated it in a second · a repair by **emphasis** where a reader never recognized it applied · a specialization with no pointer to its parent · a rule forked per domain with no evidenced miss. nitpick: a parent with no note of **why** it was split.",
    ],
  },
  {
    "file": "learner/briefs/rule.require.timeless-lessons.md.min",
    "lines": [
      "# rule.require.timeless-lessons",
      "",
      "> **a brief distills a CONCEPT. the chronicle that led to it is a DEMO of that concept, and it belongs in a file of its own.**",
      "",
      "\`\`\`",
      "$brief.md                  # the concept — fundamental, focused, free of episode",
      "$brief.example=$slug.md    # one demo — the dated, sourced episode that shows it",
      "\`\`\`",
      "",
      "a concept is timeless by nature; a demo is dated by nature. **the rule is not "delete the history" — it is "do not mix the two in one file."**",
      "",
      "## .why the MIX is the defect, not the history",
      "",
      "| the harm | how it lands |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| the **concept loses focus** | a reader who wants the pattern sifts the episode out of it, on every read |",
      "| the **demo loses its citation** | an episode buried in prose has no date, no repo, no path — it stops being checkable |",
      "| the file **grows without bound** | each round adds an episode; the concept does not get longer |",
      "",
      "## .the test — strip and re-read",
      "",
      "> **strip every temporal and session-bound word. does the claim still stand as a statement of what IS and why?**",
      "",
      "- yes → the **concept**. it stays",
      "- no → a **demo**. eject to \`example=$slug.md\`, dated and sourced",
      "- it was neither — it merely gestured at a conversation → **not a demo either.** a demo has a date, a repo, a path; a gesture has none, so there is naught to eject",
      "",
      "## .the smells — each is a demo trapped inside a concept",
      "",
      "| smell | what it is |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| *"recently"* · *"this time"* · *"we just"* · *"as we saw above"* | an episode with its citation stripped |",
      "| *"we decided"* · *"we deliberately"* · *"we chose not to"* | a deliberation the reader did not attend |",
      "| *"as discussed"* · *"per the conversation"* | a source that cannot be dereferenced |",
      "| 🔴 *"an earlier draft of this brief said…"* | the document's own version history — **not even a demo. delete it** |",
      "| *"yet"* · *"for now"* · *"not … yet"* | a schedule, and the schedule expires |",
      "| a term named **only** to say we do NOT adopt it, with no durable reason | the rejection outlives the reason |",
      "",
      "## .what an ejected demo owes",
      "",
      "the **date**, the **repo**, the **path or branch** · what happened, shortest form that stands alone · the **cost** — what it actually spent, which is what makes it evidence rather than anecdote · a pointer up to the concept.",
      "",
      "## 🟡 .a \`.reason\` file IS an ejection target — do not eject from it again",
      "",
      "a term cluster already splits along this line: \`._.choice._.md\` is the **concept** (bound in full), \`.reason.md\` is the **decision record** — dated by contract, and its dated evidence is **mandatory**. so a dated entry under \`.disputes\` or \`.evidence\` is the archetype at work, **never a smell**.",
      "",
      "🟡 what a \`.reason\` still may not hold is its **own draft history**. amend in place, or answer with a **new dated dispute**.",
      "",
      "🟡 **a verbatim wisher quote is a SEED, not a demo.** \`.said\` is verbatim by contract — never tidy a quote to satisfy this rule. its home is \`$route/.seeds/\`; a brief cites it by path.",
      "",
      "## .enforcement",
      "",
      "blocker: a brief that fuses an episode into its concept · a lesson that fails strip-and-re-read · a *"yet"* / *"for now"* / *"we decided"* in a body · a brief that narrates its **own prior drafts** (no ejection — delete it) · an ejected demo with no date, repo, or path.",
      "nitpick: a demo with no pointer up.",
      "false positive: a dated, sourced incident **inside** the concept where it is the shortest form of the claim · a verbatim \`.said\` · a dated \`.disputes\` / \`.evidence\` entry in a term \`.reason\`.",
      "",
      "⇒ the parent is \`rule.forbid.chronological-accretion\` (ehmpathy/mechanic). the peer for a route yield is \`rule.always.yield-the-output-not-the-archaeology\`.",
    ],
  },
