    "file": "learner/briefs/template.domain-term.md.min",
    "lines": [
      "# template.domain-term",
      "",
      "the shape of a \`choice._.\` cluster under \`.agent/repo=.this/role=any/briefs/domain.terms/\`. one cluster per term (one word), reused across every dobj/dop that word composes.",
      "",
      "\`\`\`",
      "term=<boundary…>.<x>._.choice._.md          # SAY — lean, always booted: the data only",
      "term=<boundary…>.<x>._.choice.reason.md     # REF — REQUIRED: etymology, disputes, evidence",
      "term=<boundary…>.<x>._.choice.example=<abc>.md   # REF — optional, one per notable example",
      "\`\`\`",
      "",
      "## .the say file — data only, no prose about the forbid",
      "",
      "🟡 **the say file carries no \`.forbid\` prose.** \`rule.forbid.domain-term-synonyms\` governs the forbid once, for all terms; the file merely lists which words are forbidden.",
      "",
      "\`\`\`md",
      "# domain.term: stone",
      "",
      "term.chosen   = stone",
      "term.kind     = noun          # noun | verb | adj",
      "term.boundary = route         # the subdomain the word holds its sense within — REQUIRED",
      "term.synonyms.forbidden:",
      "- checkpoint",
      "- waypoint",
      "",
      "## .what",
      "a single milestone on a route.",
      "",
      "## .refs",
      "- src/domain.objects/Stone.ts",
      "- src/domain.operations/route/getStone.ts",
      "",
      "## .reason",
      "- \`term=route.stone._.choice.reason.md\`",
      "- \`term=route.stone._.choice.example=<abc>.md\`",
      "\`\`\`",
      "",
      "## .the reason file — required",
      "",
      "\`\`\`md",
      "# domain.term.choice.reason: stone",
      "",
      "## .etymology",
      "why \`stone\`: a route is a *path* of markers; a stone is a marker you pass on a trail.",
      "chosen over \`checkpoint\` (implies a gate — that is the \`guard\`'s job) and \`waypoint\`",
      "(navigation jargon, not the trail metaphor).",
      "",
      "## .disputes",
      "### dispute: checkpoint — raised YYYY-MM-DD — status: RESOLVED (keep \`stone\`)",
      "- raised.by  = <traveler>",
      "- claim      = "checkpoint" reads clearer to newcomers",
      "- counter    = "checkpoint" implies a gate that VALIDATES; that concept is already",
      "               \`guard\`. a \`stone\` merely MARKS progress. to merge them overloads one",
      "               word onto two distinct concepts",
      "- resolution = keep \`stone\`; record \`checkpoint\` as a forbidden synonym",
      "",
      "## .evidence",
      "- discovery: <dimensional decomposition / scenario narrative / citation>",
      "- invariants: <forbidden combinations / states / refs, if a dobj>",
      "\`\`\`",
      "",
      "## .the example file — optional, one per occurrence",
      "",
      "\`\`\`md",
      "# domain.term.choice.example: stone — trail-marker",
      "",
      "a route is walked one stone at a time, as a hiker passes one trail-marker at a time.",
      "each stone marks *how far along* — it does not gate passage (that is the \`guard\`).",
      "\`\`\`",
      "",
      "⇒ the rules that rule the dir are named in \`domain.terms/.readme.md\`. the dispute pattern is \`howto.domain-term-disputes\`.",
      "",
      "> one word, one cluster — say lean, reason deep 📜",
    ],
  },
]
`;

