    "file": "driver/briefs/howdoes.the-review-gates-you-drive-within.md.min",
    "lines": [
      "# howdoes: the review gates you drive within",
      "",
      "**the map of the system you operate within.** a guarded stone runs its reviewers, then holds a",
      "sequence of gates. you pass once you clear them in order. each gate is an **invariant** the engine",
      "holds true by construction — its formal law is \`define.invariant.review.peer.*\`, beside this brief.",
      "",
      "\`\`\`",
      "run reviewers ─▶ 1. ABSORB gate ─▶ 2. .taken (feedback) gate ─▶ 3. threshold gate ─▶ PASS",
      "                    (per concern)      (per reviewer)              (stone-wide tally)",
      "\`\`\`",
      "",
      "all three gates are conditions of ONE root law, \`passage\`: \`PASS ⟺ every guard terminal ∧ every",
      "counted concern absorbed ∧ residual tally under allowance\`.",
      "",
      "| # | gate | what it demands of you | law (a \`passage\` condition) |",
      "|---|---|---|---|",
      "| 1 | **absorb** | a disposition — \`disputed\` or \`conceded\` — on EACH concern a rejected reviewer raised | \`absorb\` (b) |",
      "| 2 | **the \`.taken\`** | your argument to the reviewer, per reviewer — accepted only once #1 is done | \`absorb\`, added gate (b) |",
      "| 3 | **threshold** | the stone-wide tally of residual concerns falls under its allowance | \`budget.urgent-earns-budget\` (c) |",
      "",
      "## the five laws — what each requires of you",
      "",
      "- 🔴 **ABSORB** — \`feedbackAbsorbed(given) ⟺ every concern within it absorbed\`. to absorb the feedback",
      "  is the \`.taken\`, and it is REFUSED until each concern within it carries a disposition. a fix is not",
      "  an absorption — the debt keys to the concern, so declare on it. one \`--as disputed|conceded\` per",
      "  concern, THEN the \`.taken\`.",
      "- **PASSAGE** — \`PASS ⟺ every peer guard terminal\`. a \`rejected\` lane is NOT terminal; it holds the",
      "  road. approval is permission; passage is your explicit \`--as passed\`. work every reviewer to",
      "  terminal before a human is pulled.",
      "- **DISPUTABLE** — a concern that COUNTS toward the tally is yours to dispute, approved lane or",
      "  rejected lane alike (the tally sums stone-wide). OWED ≠ PERMITTED: you are FORCED to absorb only a",
      "  rejected lane's concerns; you MAY dispute any that counts — an approved lane's nitpick among them.",
      "- **EXHAUSTED** — exhaustion unlocks the LEVEL; it does not discharge the DEBT. answer an exhausted",
      "  reviewer's blocker even though it can never re-run. levers: a \`.taken\`, a budget top-up, or a human.",
      "- **BUDGET** — a budget hit needs a human ⟺ a live \`urgent\` concession stands. grade every concession",
      "  (\`--severity better|urgent\`) by the harm test: name the harm that ships if unfixed → \`urgent\`;",
      "  else \`better\` (never earns budget).",
      "",
      "> **absorb each concern, answer each reviewer, hold the tally under the floor — and only a human",
      "> grants what only a human can.** the gates are the system; the invariants are why they hold.",
      "",
      "⇒ see also: \`define.invariant.review.peer.absorb\` · \`.passage\` · \`.exhausted\` ·",
      "\`.absorption.disputable-regardless-of-verdict\` · \`.budget.urgent-earns-budget\` ·",
      "\`howdoes.a-concern-travels-from-reviewer-to-absorption\` · \`rule.always.absorb-every-concern\`.",
    ],
  },
