    "file": "driver/briefs/rule.always.absorb-every-concern.md.min",
    "lines": [
      "# rule.always.absorb-every-concern",
      "",
      "> **you have not absorbed a reviewer's feedback until you absorb EACH concern within it. one",
      "> disposition per concern — disputed or conceded — or the road does not pass.**",
      "",
      "a **concern** = one blocker or one nitpick a reviewer enumerated. to **absorb** it = render its",
      "disposition with its argument: \`disputed\` (fine to continue — cite a fulcrum) or \`conceded\` (the",
      "reviewer is right — commit to fix). absorb the feedback = absorb every concern within it.",
      "",
      "⇒ the law: \`define.invariant.review.peer.absorb\` — \`feedbackAbsorbed(given) ⟺ ∀ concern : absorbed(concern)\`.",
      "",
      "## 🔴 .two grains, one verb — the coarse gated on the fine",
      "",
      "| act | grain | what it is |",
      "|---|---|---|",
      "| absorb a concern | one concern | a disposition (dispute\\|concede) + argument |",
      "| absorb the feedback | the given | the \`.taken\` — the reviewer as a whole |",
      "",
      "🔴 **the added gate: the \`.taken\` is REFUSED until each concern within it is absorbed.** absorb-the-feedback",
      "is COMPOSED of absorb-each-concern — the \`.taken\` is not retired, it gains a precondition.",
      "",
      "| disposition | commits you to | argument lives in |",
      "|---|---|---|",
      "| \`conceded\` — the default | fix it, run again | an optional \`--why\`, or the fix |",
      "| \`disputed\` — the escalation | shed from the tally; council rules | the fulcrum \`--why\` names — **required** |",
      "",
      "🟡 concede-and-fix is the default; dispute is an escalation (severe or recurs) — never to skip the fix.",
      "",
      "\`\`\`",
      "rhx route.stone.set --stone <s> --as conceded --with <reviewer> --about <concern> --severity better|urgent",
      "rhx route.stone.set --stone <s> --as disputed  --with <reviewer> --about <concern> --why <fulcrum-path>",
      "\`\`\`",
      "",
      "\`--about\` names ONE concern by ordinal (\`blocker.3\`); no \`--about all\`. ordinals renumber each generation; re-absorb what the given now says.",
      "",
      "| when… | then… |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| a given rejects | every concern it enumerates owes an absorption before the round passes |",
      "| you would write the \`.taken\` for the reviewer "as a whole" | absorb each concern FIRST — the \`.taken\` is refused until you do. the whole is gated on its parts |",
      "| you fix the code and re-arrive | 🔴 a fix is not an absorption. the debt keys to the concern — declare on it, or the gate holds |",
      "| an approved lane's nitpick pushes the stone over the floor | you MAY absorb it — the judge tallies stone-wide |",
      "| the halt names concerns un-absorbed | those are the atoms owed. one command each |",
      "",
      "test: **for every concern enumerated, did you render a disposition on THAT concern?** every one → the",
      "feedback is absorbed · one un-absorbed → the road holds and the halt names it.",
      "",
      "boundary: a concern with no hold owes none — a forgiven level, a lane that never spoke, an unreadable",
      "given (a malfunction → re-run, never an absorption; \`F030\`).",
      "",
      "blocker: a passage sought while any enumerated concern of a given that counts is un-absorbed · a code",
      "fix re-arrived as though it discharged a concern · a disposition on the reviewer as a whole rather",
      "than per concern · a dispute with no fulcrum \`--why\`.",
      "",
      "⇒ see also: \`define.invariant.review.peer.absorb\` · \`rule.always.concede-with-a-severity\` ·",
      "\`rule.forbid.suppression-of-undeclared-concerns\` · \`rule.always.converge-with-reviewers._\`.",
    ],
  },
  {
    "file": "driver/briefs/rule.always.archive-the-wishers-words-verbatim.md.min",
    "lines": [
      "# rule.always.archive-the-wishers-words-verbatim",
      "",
      "when the wisher says a word that **changes the work**, catch it verbatim before you distill it.",
      "",
      "\`\`\`",
      "$route/.seeds/inventory.of=seeds._.md                # the SUMMARY — the axis, the counts, the gaps",
      "$route/.seeds/inventory.of=seeds.case=S$n-$slug.md   # one ENTRY per utterance",
      "\`\`\`",
      "",
      "both are owed, every time.",
      "",
      "| when the wisher… | then |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| settles a question | archive it — future rounds inherit the settlement |",
      "| 🔴 **corrects you** | the highest-value quote there is: it records the wrong path AND the right one |",
      "| coins a word or a convention | the coinage's source is its etymology |",
      "| specifies a contract verbatim — a path, a flag, a format | a specification paraphrased is a specification changed |",
      "| 🔴 **asks a question** whose answer changes the work | the cheapest kind to lose — in hindsight it reads as though YOU found the gap |",
      "| — or you are about to write *"the wisher asked for…"* | that citation needs a source. archive first |",
      "",
      "a seed holds \`.said\` · \`.settled\` · \`.landed\`.",
      "",
      "| repair it | never touch it |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| a **typo** — a transposed letter, a dropped one, a doubled word | a word choice, however informal |",
      "| **profanity** — cut it, or swap in a neutral \`[placeholder]\`. never a softened or masked form of the word | the order the points arrive in |",
      "| a mangled path, flag, or identifier, where the intent is plain | a mid-thought correction — that IS the record |",
      "",
      "🟡 **\`.said\` is verbatim in SUBSTANCE — repair the surface.** the words, their order, their emphasis, and their mid-thought corrections stay unedited; **typos and profanity are repaired.**",
