    "file": "driver/briefs/rule.always.bear-every-self-review.md.min",
    "lines": [
      "# rule.always.bear-every-self-review",
      "",
      "> **a self review cannot be overridden. it is borne and carried out — as many honest reviews as it takes. there are no shortcuts.**",
      "",
      "✅ **the absence is mechanical.** every overrule operation lives under \`guard/review/peer/\`; \`guard/review/self/\` has not one. there is no lever to reach for, so the ask must never be made.",
      "",
      "🔴 **the count is the WORK, never a budget.**",
      "",
      "| the peer ladder | the self ladder |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| a budget, spent down · exhaustion is terminal · **and a debt per blocker beside it** | a debt only · no exhaustion, only an unpaid remainder |",
      "| a human may overrule it | no one may |",
      "| more rounds cost the human's attention | more reviews cost only yours |",
      "",
      "🔴 **the guard holds you for NO duration, and that is not a permission.** \`patience, friend\` is a cue, not a gate: what the guard permits and what you owe are two different quantities.",
      "",
      "| when… | then… |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| the count **grows** | more work found, not a defect. carry it — do NOT diagnose the guard |",
      "| you would ask a human to **waive** one | there is no lever to grant it |",
      "| \`patience, friend\` renders and you promise again at once | 🔴 it cost naught to ignore — which is why it tests you, never the guard. read the four cues |",
      "| the promise cleared on the **first** try | the design, never a signal you reviewed enough. the clock went because it charged the thorough driver, not because the bar fell |",
      "| you **repair the artifact** mid-review | 🔴 do it. the trigger is keyed \`(stone, slug)\` — no repair re-triggers a review or restarts a clock |",
      "| \`--as blocked\` because the ladder feels long | length is not a wall. the only lever here is your attention |",
      "",
      "test, per review: **"what did I find, and what did I settle?"** — a repair, or a reasoned hold with evidence. **neither → you did not review. begin again.**",
      "",
      "blocker: a promise with no honest articulation · an articulation that names neither a repair nor a hold · a promise made because the guard would let it through · an ask to waive or override · a count that grows, reported as a malfunction · a self review **batched**, every repair held until the promise clears (the clock that made that rational is gone).",
    ],
  },
