    "lines": [
      "# rule.always.converge-to-terminal",
      "",
      "work every reviewer to a terminal verdict before a human is pulled. a level is terminal when every reviewer at it is \`approved\`, \`exhausted\`, \`malfunction\`, or \`constraint\`.",
      "",
      "| the level did | you must |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| approve | continue — the next level is already live |",
      "| exhaust (earned) | continue — the next level runs. 🟡 **and answer any blocker it left** |",
      "| reject, budget left | converge: fix, or articulate why it holds, then re-arrive |",
      "| every level terminal | now, and only now, a human may overrule |",
      "",
      "## 🔴 exhaustion unlocks the LEVEL. it does not discharge the DEBT",
      "",
      "| exhaustion does | exhaustion does NOT |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| make the level terminal, so the next runs | close a blocker it raised before its budget ran out |",
      "| free you from further rounds *with that reviewer* | free you from the \`.taken\` you owe it |",
      "",
      "**the debt is keyed to the reviewer, never to the generation of the code it read.** so an exhausted reviewer whose blocker you never answered holds the **stone** — the unlock frees the *ladder* — and the entrance gate refuses the next round meanwhile. ⇒ that is what gives a manufactured exhaustion a real price. your levers: **answer it**, plus a **budget top-up** if the reviewer must re-read to confirm. a human overrule is the third, and the only one that needs a human.",
      "",
      "**exhaustion is earned, never casual.**",
      "",
      "- budget burned without genuine engagement is a coast, and a defect",
      "- an exhausted level owes a record in \`.taken.by_self\`",
      "  - what you tried each round",
      "  - what would fix that reviewer for the next traveler",
      "- ⇒ an exhausted level with no record is indistinguishable from a coast",
      "",
      "🟡 re-arrival is cheap — the guard reuses any reviewer that returned 0 blockers, keyed on the artifact hash. read \`howdoes.the-guard-caches-a-clean-reviewer-by-artifact-hash\` before you judge an iteration too costly to spend.",
    ],
