      "## a malfunctioned reviewer still owes you a \`.taken\`",
      "",
      "a repair alone does not re-open the door. the fix changes the code; the debt is keyed to the reviewer, so it stands until you answer it. the halt prompt names the \`.taken\` path — a malfunction is dischargeable, never a deadlock. the reviewer malfunctioned; you are still the party that must say so.",
      "",
      "## the overflowed reviewer — narrow it in the guard",
      "",
      "\`\`\`sh",
      "rhx route.mutate grant get     # the guard edit needs the route's mutate grant — a human grants it once",
      "# then edit $route/<stone>.guard directly: narrow that reviewer's \`--paths-with\`, add a",
      "# \`--paths-wout\`, and/or trim its \`--conversation\` depth. then re-arrive and let the GUARD run it.",
      "\`\`\`",
      "",
      "🟡 no \`rhx\` command edits a guard: \`route.mutate.guard\` is the PreToolUse hook that seals \`*.guard\` until \`$route/.route/.privilege.mutate.flag\` exists — a gate, never an editor. blocked → the one ask of the human is \`rhx route.mutate grant allow\`; the edit after it is yours.",
      "",
      "## the bind arithmetic — what a guard bind needs",
      "",
      "the inherited scope is correct — do not re-derive it. \`getAllFileChangesFromRange.ts\` prefers \`origin/main\` (\`getOneMainBranch\`) and takes \`git merge-base\` (\`getOneBaseArgs\`), so a commit main is ahead on cannot enter the diff. an item a correctly-bound reviewer raises is yours.",
      "",
      "\`--paths-with <glob>\` includes, \`--paths-wout <glob>\` excludes (alias \`--paths-without\`); both repeat, so a wide lane narrows by exclusion — the commonest cut is the test corpus a production rubric does not grade:",
      "",
      "\`\`\`",
      "--paths-with 'src/**/*' --paths-wout '**/*.test.ts' --paths-wout '**/__snapshots__/**'",
      "\`\`\`",
      "",
      "a brace in either slot works — \`'**/*.{ts,md}'\` and \`'{src,blackbox}/**'\` alike. read what a bind matched from the scope block's \`paths.with\` / \`paths.wout\` lines and the \`joined via\` count.",
      "an unknown flag refuses as a constraint and names itself, so a misspelled bind fails loud. a narrowed lane that overflows at the same file count as before means the glob matched what it did before — read the scope block.",
      "",
      "## which lever — read it off the refusal's \`lever\` branch, never a hand census",
      "",
      "| the refusal says | the lever |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| targets mostly **edited** | narrow the bind — \`--paths-wout '<heavy>/**'\` |",
      "| targets mostly **additions** | declare the whole set once — \`rhx route.guard.partition --for review --peer @all --partition '<slug>=<globs>' ...\`, through vertical domains (\`rule.forbid.horizontal-partitions\`). new work the lane must read; to cut it hides it |",
      "| targets hold **no** mass | narrow \`--rules\`, \`--refs\`, or \`--conversation\` |",
      "| a **partition** still overflows alone | narrow that partition, or split it in two — the tool never splits twice |",
