    "lines": [
      "# rule.always.spend-own-levers-before-escalation",
      "",
      "a halt is a diagnosis to make, not a message to relay. the guard prints what *would* unblock the stone; it never says **who owns each lever**. sort by owner and spend yours first.",
      "",
      "| lever | owner |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| \`rhx route.stone.set --as absorbed --that <reviewer>\` — converge; a spent meter discharges no debt | **driver** |",
      "| 🔴 a direct edit of \`$route/<stone>.guard\` — that lane's \`--paths-wout\` / \`--paths-with\`, its \`--conversation\` depth, its \`level\` | **driver**, once the route's mutate grant stands |",
      "| a diagnosed reviewer malfunction — absent credential, bad glob, stale supply | **driver** |",
      "| 🔴 \`rhx route.guard.budget --for review --add N --stone <stone>\` | **driver, ONLY with a warrant** — see below |",
      "| the route's mutate grant (\`rhx route.mutate grant allow\`) · \`--as approved\` · \`--as overruled\` · the commit quota · a **credential** the keyrack reports \`absent\` · release auth | human |",
      "",
      "🟡 **no \`rhx\` command edits a guard.** \`route.mutate.guard\` is the PreToolUse hook that seals \`*.stone\` / \`*.guard\` / \`.route/**\` — a gate, never an editor. the act is a plain edit of the \`.guard\` file, permitted once \`$route/.route/.privilege.mutate.flag\` exists. \`rhx route.mutate grant get\` first: granted → edit now · not granted → ask the human for that one grant per route, then the edit is yours.",
      "",
      "⛔ **a hand-run \`rhx review\` is NOT on this table, deliberately.** it draws no budget, so it is no lever at all (\`rule.forbid.hand-run-reviews\`). ⇒ the guard row above is what a driver who reaches for it actually wants.",
      "",
      "🟡 **adjacency is the trap** — two remedies side by side with no owner column read as two human remedies. the budget halt names its owners and sorts the driver's first, but **which** lever that is turns on what the last round conceded: \`increase budget — yours to spend\` on an urgent concession, \`fix what you conceded — yours to run\` on a better one, \`converge with the reviewer — yours to run\` where naught was conceded. 🔴 a malfunction, a self-review gate, and a judge threshold each print a remedy list with no owner column, so the sort stays yours to perform.",
      "",
      "## 🔴 budget is the ALLOWANCE, and it is scarce past its bound",
      "",
      "**the grant is refused by default**, so a top-up is yours **only with a warrant**.",
      "",
      "> **inside the meter, taste counts. past the meter, only harm does.**",
      "",
      "all three conjuncts are owed:",
      "",
      "| the conjunct | what it refuses |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| a **live urgent concession** on the stone | a round bought on a wish to continue |",
      "| a **target reviewer that has run dry** | a pad taken before the bound bites |",
      "| a \`--stone\` that named **one** stone | one warrant spent across a prefix's worth of stones |",
      "",
      "\`\`\`sh",
      "rhx route.stone.set --stone <s> --as conceded --with <reviewer> --about <concern> --severity urgent",
      "rhx route.guard.budget --for review --add N --peer <reviewer> --stone <s>",
      "\`\`\`",
      "",
      "🟡 **grade by the harm test, never by what you want the meter to say.** \`urgent\` is the closed set — security · safety · monetary · reputation · behavioral, with a harm you can name. all else is \`better\`, and \`better\` earns no round past the meter (\`rule.always.concede-with-a-severity\`).",
      "",
      "🔴 **and \`--add N\` does NOT extend every reviewer on the stone.** a bare add lands on the **latest level alone**; a lower level stays exhausted unless \`--level\` or \`--peer\` names it (F022 fork E).",
      "",
      "🟡 **exhaustion is still often not what it looks like** — a reviewer that spent its round to RAISE a blocker has none left to CONFIRM your fix, so it shows \`exhausted 🌙\` with blockers listed that are already closed. **where that blocker named a real harm, grade it \`urgent\` and the round is yours.** where it named taste, the fix IS the whole remedy.",
      "",
      "🟡 a human may grant regardless — to reach for that before you have tried to converge is the very escalation this rule forbids.",
      "",
      "the test: **"is there a command i could run right now that would move this stone?"**",
      "yes → run it. no → surface it, with the exact command the human must run.",
