    "lines": [
      "# rule.forbid.hand-run-reviews",
      "",
      "> **a driver never runs \`rhx review\` by hand. a review is summoned by the guard, or it does not happen.**",
      "",
      "no scoped re-run, no diagnostic sweep, no "second opinion", no probe. **the invocation is the violation** — the flags and the motive do not enter into it.",
      "",
      "## 🔴 .the harm — the party under review picks its own reviewer",
      "",
      "| the guard's lane | a hand-run review |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| rubric, bind, brain, focus — declared in the \`.guard\` | **all chosen at the prompt, by the driver** |",
      "| costs a budget round | costs zero |",
      "| mints a \`.given\` the judge tallies | mints no artifact the engine reads |",
      "| its verdict gates the stone | its verdict gates naught |",
      "",
      "⇒ **the identical defect \`rule.forbid.commits-the-route-did-not-ask-for\` names**: a commit changes *what the reviewers see*; a hand-run review changes *who reviews and under what terms*. **no reviewer consented to either.**",
      "",
      "## .what to do instead — the lever is the GUARD",
      "",
      "| the situation | the sanctioned move |",
      "|---|---|",
      "| a lane **overflowed** its window | 🔴 edit \`$route/<stone>.guard\` directly — narrow its \`--paths-wout\` / \`--paths-with\`, or trim its \`--conversation\`. **then let the guard run it**. needs the route's mutate grant (\`rhx route.mutate grant get\`; a human grants it once) |",
      "| a lane's bind is **wrong** | the same. the bind is a guard field, and the guard is yours |",
      "| a lane is **out of budget** | \`rhx route.guard.budget --for review --add N\` |",
      "| a rubric wants a **different** corpus | that is a new lane. add it to the guard |",
      "| you want a **second opinion** | \`rule.always.get-a-second-opinion-before-foreman\` — enroll a peer ROLE, never a hand-run lane |",
      "",
      "test: **"am I about to invoke \`rhx review\`?"** — yes → 🔴 **stop.** the answer is a guard edit. there is no second question.",
      "",
      "blocker: a \`rhx review\` invoked by a driver, for any reason · a scoped re-run cited as a spent lever · a hand-run verdict cited as evidence a lane is clean · an overflowed lane left unrepaired because the guard edit was believed to be the wisher's.",
    ],
  },
